



td [-_e[s]] [file] ;  display GPS on a Triple X

Input is the output from a GPS translator.
Output is escape codes for a Triple X. If file is not defined
then input is taken from the default input.

Options:

     e         Enlarge one region of GPS universe to fill the
	       Triple X screen. If s is present then region
	       number s is displayed. The default region is 13.

Example:   td -e A.g
displays A.g. The viewing window is built to display region 13 only.
